# Standalone Host — VPS environment
#
# Copy to /etc/lotus-host.env (0600, owned by the user the unit runs as) and edit.
# systemd reads this file directly; nothing here is a shell script, so no `export`,
# no quotes-with-spaces tricks, and no variable expansion.
#
# Every name below is read by packages/host/src/** (LOTUS_PAIR_ADDRESS by deploy/pair.sh).
# Anything not listed here is not configuration — it is a default the code owns.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Starts the embedded host instead of delegating to a desktop app (src/index.ts).
# Also what runs sessions in lotus-sessiond, so they survive a restart (ADR-0067).
LOTUS_MODE=standalone

# The only network-facing listener. Keep it on loopback: ADR-C reaches this host
# through the private path the machine already has (a Cloudflare Tunnel route on
# devbox-vps), never by opening a port. A malformed value falls back to
# 127.0.0.1:8787 rather than to 0.0.0.0 — a typo cannot expose the host.
LOTUS_MOBILE_BIND=127.0.0.1:8787

# Bearer for the loopback-only admin surface (/admin/health, /admin/pairing-code,
# /admin/devices). WITHOUT IT THERE IS NO ADMIN SURFACE AT ALL — the adapter starts
# without one rather than serving it unauthenticated, which also means no pairing
# code and no way to check health. install.sh generates one if you leave it blank.
LOTUS_MOBILE_ADMIN_SECRET=

# ── Strongly recommended ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Firebase service account JSON that lets this host wake a backgrounded phone.
# Without it `hostCaps` honestly omits `push` — and an approval waiting on the VPS
# is never announced. On a machine nobody watches that is indistinguishable from
# nothing happening, which is why the host warns loudly at boot (startup-warnings.ts).
# Copy ~/.lotus/fcm-service-account.json from the desktop machine; chmod 600.
LOTUS_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=/home/YOU/.lotus/fcm-service-account.json

# What the operator sees as this host's name in Pocket, and its `hostId`.
# Defaults to the machine hostname, which is usually the wrong kind of true.
LOTUS_HOST_LABEL=vps

# What a phone dials to reach this host, for the QR `deploy/pair.sh` prints. Read by that
# script only — the host itself never needs to know it. Leave unset when the phone dials
# LOTUS_MOBILE_BIND directly (a tailnet IP); set it when that bind is loopback behind a
# tunnel, because a QR pointing at 127.0.0.1 sends the phone to itself.
# LOTUS_PAIR_ADDRESS=https://pocket.example.com

# ── Projects ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where agent-cloned repos land and where the project registry looks. Created if
# missing. Defaults to ~/lotus-workspaces.
PROJECTS_ROOT=/home/YOU/lotus-workspaces

# Extra directories a paired phone may browse, PATH-style. The workspace root above is
# always open; this adds the places you keep repositories that did not come from a clone.
#
# It is a jail, and it is the only one: what is not named here cannot be listed from the
# phone, and nothing here ever serves a file's contents — only directory names. Leave it
# empty and the phone sees the workspace root alone.
#
# LOTUS_BROWSE_ROOTS=/home/YOU/kerja:/srv/repos


# An explicit project list instead of a scanned root. Setting this suppresses the
# PROJECTS_ROOT default, so set one or the other, not both by accident.
# PROJECTS_JSON=/home/YOU/.lotus/projects.json

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Headless Director is ON by default and spawns `claude` plus the MCP sidecar.
# Set to `off` for a plain remote-control host — worth doing on the first deploy, so
# a failure has one cause instead of two.
# DIRECTOR_PROVIDER=off

# The sidecar is launched as `bun` on PATH. systemd units do not run a login shell,
# so a bun installed under ~/.bun is NOT on PATH here: give the absolute path.
# LOTUS_MCP_SIDECAR_CMD=/home/YOU/.bun/bin/bun

# Overrides the sessiond/node-pty choice. Leave unset. `node-pty` here means sessions
# die with the host — the one thing this deployment exists to prevent.
# LOTUS_PTY=sessiond

# A lotus-sessiond binary to run instead of the one embedded in lotus-host. Leave unset.
# LOTUS_SESSIOND_BIN=/home/YOU/lotus-sessiond

# State directory: devices, session logs, diagnostics, admin advert. Default ~/.lotus.
# LOTUS_STATE_DIR=/home/YOU/.lotus

# Swarm task store. Default <state dir>/standalone-tasks.
# TASKS_DIR=/home/YOU/.lotus/standalone-tasks

# Turns off the session-history measurement counters.
# LOTUS_DIAGNOSTICS=0

# ── Deliberately absent ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# LOTUS_API_KEY / LOTUS_API_URL — client-mode only. A standalone host mints its own
#   key at boot and hands it straight to its own ApiClient. Setting them here does
#   nothing except mislead the next reader.
# SERVER_PORT — not read by anything. The embedded server binds port 0 on loopback
#   and passes the assigned port in-process; there is no port to choose.
